  "base_address": "Defined at SoC level; offsets given relative to module base.",
  "notes": "QSPI/OSPI is command-oriented: opcodes (0x00..0xFF) select read / program / erase / status / configuration functions accessed through the instruction-address-dummy-data phase protocol. xSPI adds a volatile/non-volatile configuration-register interface; the legacy Status Register WIP/WEL bits are the primary program/erase handshake. Memory itself is a linear byte address space (3 or 4 byte address).",
